<title>USA: Federated merchandising unit chief resigns.</title>
<headline>Federated merchandising unit chief resigns.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federated Department Stores Inc said on Monday that W. Jay Carothers has resigned as president of its New York-based Federated Merchandising Group effective June 19 to accept another position outside of the company.</p>
<p>Federated said it expects to name a successor shortly.</p>
<p>In the interim, functions previously reporting to Carothers will report to Terry Lundgren, Federated's president and chief merchandising officer, the company said.</p>
</text>
